---
Read the repository the project is in, with no git program: its place, HEAD, revisions, status and configuration, as JSON (ADR 0339)

Usage: specforge git <COMMAND>

Commands:
  repo    Where the repository is: its top directory, git directory and common directory
  head    HEAD's commit and branch, whether it is detached or unborn, and its upstream
  rev     What each revision names: its sha and kind, or that it names nothing
  status  The working tree's status: each changed, conflicted and untracked path, and whether it is clean
  config  Every value a configuration key has, and the one git applies
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
